  "_digits": "What an amount FIELD keeps. Sean, 2026-08-21: \"don't show the - in the input field and only allow numbers to be typed.\" So the field holds digits and at most one dot and nothing else — a typed minus is not a sign any more, it is simply refused, and the sign lives in the − button beside the field and nowhere else. That is the OPPOSITE of the rule this replaced, which had the minus key and the minus button as the same action. Rows are [what arrived, what the field keeps].",
